# Aero Window — nightly reboot (4 AM local).
# Installed to /etc/cron.d/aero-nightly-reboot by deploy/pi/install.sh.
#
# Rationale:
#   - Chromium leaks a few MB per hour of WebGL use; a fresh Chromium avoids
#     GPU-context starvation after ~72h.
#   - systemd + the kiosk service brings the app back up in <30s.
#   - 04:00 is after the dim-schedule fires at 02:00 and before the
#     bright-schedule at 06:00, so the reboot happens while the display is dim.
#   - Waits (up to 50 min) for a running OTA first. A reboot mid-build left
#     HEAD at the new commit with no build/ — every later poll said "already
#     up to date" and the pane stayed dark. The updater now repairs that too,
#     but not racing it is cheaper than repairing it.
#
# Format: m h dom mon dow user command
# (A running Type=oneshot unit reports `activating`, which `is-active --quiet`
#  treats as inactive — hence the prefix match, not the exit code.)
0 4 * * * root /bin/bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 50); do [[ "$(systemctl is-active aero-updater.service 2>/dev/null)" == activ* ]] || break; sleep 60; done; /sbin/shutdown -r now'
